Subject: pcsx2-gsrunner: -vif1, a ROR_GSDUMP_VIF1 dump through VIF1 + microVU1 (MTVU) + GS without VMManager::Initialize

Rule of Rose port, renderer plan step 0b (notes/renderer.md 6.8). On top of 0001. The VM memory map, microVU1 + the
VIF unpackers, the VU1/VIF1/GIF resets and MTGS are brought up by hand; per loop the dump's GS state, its VU1 state
(record 0x40, loaded through the VU thread), its VIF1 input streams (record 0x41) into VIF1transfer and its PATH3
transfers into the GIF unit. PATH1/PATH2 records are skipped: VIF1 and VU1 produce them. -vif1-nofeed drops the VIF1
streams (control run). Two pieces of VMManager's CPU-thread init/shutdown are needed: x86Emitter::use_avx (else
microVU's AVX2 block compare is emitted without VEX, never matches, and microVU recompiles forever) and
SysMemory::Release at exit (else SharedMemoryMappingArea asserts). Against PCSX2 v2.8.2 (fd9d310).

